  learned each and every line
  
1. spark.read

Used to read files into Spark.

spark.read

It creates a DataFrame reader object.

2. \ (Backslash)

Backslash means:

“Continue code in next line”

Without \, Python thinks statement ended.

Example:

a = 10 + \
20
3. .option("header","true")

Tells Spark:

First row contains column names

Example file:

id|name|age
101|Ravi|25

Spark will use:

id
name
age

as column names.

If false:

.option("header","false")

Spark creates default columns:

_c0, _c1, _c2
4. .option("inferSchema","true")

Automatically detects datatype.

Example:

Value	Detected Type
101	Integer
25.5	Double
Ravi	String

Without inferSchema:

Everything becomes string.

Example

Without inferSchema:

"101"
"25"

With inferSchema:

101
25

(integer type)

5. .csv()

Reads CSV/text file.

.csv("path")
6. File Path
"/Volumes/my_files/my_filesschema/csv_files/my_files/Pipe CSV.txt"

Location of file in Databricks Volume.

7. sep="|"

Separator/delimiter used in file.

Your file looks like:

111|Rohit|24|Male

Here separator is |.

So Spark splits columns using pipe symbol.
